 "notes": "48 cells (3 frozen controllers x 4 reset conditions x 4 fresh manifests, 6,144 episodes), no fitting, no model calls. One cell died at simulator start-up with the known allocator crash (malloc: unaligned tcache chunk) before writing anything; the driver was rerun and resumed at that cell, as documented for this crash; no completed cell was rerun. CONFIRMATORY: JOINT under tilt-only 1.5x minus JOINT under position-and-joints-only 1.5x on 512 identical cases: -0.139, paired 95% interval [-0.189, -0.089] (manifest-clustered [-0.164, -0.113]; 283 vs 354 successes; 54 wins, 125 losses). The interval excludes zero, so tilt scaling is clearly the more damaging perturbation, but it crosses the registered -0.15: INCONCLUSIVE on the registered magnitude. Descriptive: against nominal (0.777), JOINT loses 0.225 [-0.272, -0.177] under tilt-only, 0.086 [-0.130, -0.042] under position-only and 0.316 under both (0.461, reproducing D-089's full 1.5x result on new cases); the two effects are roughly additive. Tilt-only also costs the PPO expert 0.105 (0.998 -> 0.893; position-only costs it 0.008) and D-072 0.104, so wider initial tilt is harder for every controller; JOINT loses about twice as much as either. Under tilt-only JOINT's early drops rise from 27 to 60 of 512 and persistent-slow failures from 64 to 86. Delivery (reconstructed): mean initial tilt 0.599 rad nominal and position-only, 0.895 rad tilt-only and full; position and joint draws unchanged under tilt-only. Limits: one frozen lineage, one scale, position and joint draws scaled together, 512 pairs."
